        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Seven years ago, a madman attempted to assassinate you and every Republican in Congress.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "People are glorifying the assassin of Brian Thompson.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker has heard about the glorification of the assassin on air.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The leader’s survival makes them a symbol of resilience worth emulating.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Glorifying an assassin undermines justice and moral order.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Public discourse should reflect respect for victims and their survivors.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker expects the leader to have strong emotional and ethical reactions to such glorification.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "The audience values moral leadership and public accountability.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      },
      {
        "text": "Media coverage plays a significant role in shaping public attitudes toward violence and perpetrators.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Clarification Request (Specific)"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 50690,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50690.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "It's disgusting. You, I mean, You know, when you try to justify or equivocate, you know, what somebody did to take another life, I mean, here's a man with a family. You know, you have an issue with what happens at a company or a government. You have the right to go petition to make your case, to vote people out of office, to run for office. But violence is never an answer. Violence should never be condoned and it surely shouldn't be glorified. And to see this, you know, and it just shows you how there's such a leftist tilt that the value of life just seems to be diminished by so many people. And it's important for us to push back. We can never allow that to become a norm, you know, where we're in here in America. That is something that somebody can act like is an acceptable behavior.",
